module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.FibredGroupoidLimitPreserving
public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.OpenModuliSubstack
public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpaceMorphismProperties
public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.EnlargedEtaleRingedSite
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.FiniteType
import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.FinitePresentation
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.SpaceLocalPropertiesChartTest
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.SpaceEtalePresentationPropertyCriterion
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.SchemeEtaleSourceTargetProperties

/-! # Limit preservation makes representable Isom spaces locally of finite type

Source: Stacks Project, Artin's Axioms, Tags 0CXI and 0CXM, first proof paragraph;
Criteria for Representability, Tag 06CX
(blueprint: lem-sfb-limit-preserving-isom-space-lft).

An algebraic space over T is encoded by an algebraic space over S with a map to h_T.
The Isom representation is natural for every choice of pullback lifts. The second
statement retains both projections of the space of triples. Products in Over S are
scheme fibre products over S. No stack descent or Noetherian hypothesis is imposed.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v w

open AlgebraicGeometry AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace Opposite
open CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace CategoryTheory

/-- Every algebraic space representing a fibrewise Isom functor is locally of finite type
when the fibred groupoid is limit preserving and has representable diagonal.

Source: Stacks Project, Artin's Axioms, Tag 0CXI (lemma-diagonal), with the explicit
Isom identification; Criteria for Representability, Tag 06CX
(blueprint: lem-sfb-limit-preserving-isom-space-lft).

The hypothesis hI is the representing bijection, natural under all further pullback
lifts, as in the existing dm_isom_space_unramified interface. The diagonal hypothesis
is the existing equivalent formulation of representability of every Isom presheaf.

Proof: (1) The fibre of the diagonal over a pair (a,b) consists of triples (c,u,v).
The functor (c,u,v) maps to v composed with the inverse of u; its inverse sends delta
to (a,id,delta). Arrows of triples are unique when they exist, and exist exactly when
the resulting isomorphisms agree. This identifies the diagonal fibre with the Isom
presheaf, naturally in the base scheme.
(2) Apply lem-sfb-representable-lfp-object-limit-test to the diagonal. For a directed
affine limit, write gamma=(u,v). Isomorphism descent gives delta_j descending v/u.
Take c_j=a_j, alpha=u inverse, beta=(id,delta_j). Then gamma composed with the diagonal
of alpha equals beta at the limit, which is precisely relative object descent.
(3) The criterion gives local finite presentation on compatible etale charts. A
finitely presented algebra is finitely generated by the images of its polynomial
variables. Thus the same charts give local finite type, using
lem-sfb-space-local-properties-chart-test. Transport through the specified natural
representation hI to the arbitrary representing space I. Empty bases cause no exception.
(4) For the fibre-product consequences below, take the Isom space of the two pulled-back
objects over U times_S V. Base change and composition give both projections locally
of finite type (lem-sfb-stack-finite-type-calculus). The every-presentation clause of
lem-sfb-space-etale-presentation-property-criterion, with identity target charts,
gives both composites from every etale scheme chart, without surjectivity. -/
theorem limit_preserving_isom_space_locallyOfFiniteType {S : Scheme.{u}}
    (F : BasedCategory.{v, w} (Over S)) (hF : IsFibredInGroupoids F)
    (hLimits : FibredGroupoidLimit.IsLimitPreserving F)
    (hDiagonal : HasAlgebraicSpaceDiagonal F)
    (T : Over S) (x y : Functor.Fiber F.p T)
    (I : AlgebraicSpace S) (p : I.obj.obj ⟶ yoneda.obj T)
    (hI : ∃ e : ∀ (U : Over S) (q : U ⟶ T) (xU yU : Functor.Fiber F.p U)
        (a : xU.val ⟶ x.val) (b : yU.val ⟶ y.val),
        F.p.IsHomLift q a → F.p.IsHomLift q b →
        {z : I.obj.obj.obj (op U) // p.app (op U) z = q} ≃ (xU ≅ yU),
      ∀ (U U' : Over S) (f : U' ⟶ U) (q : U ⟶ T)
        (xU yU : Functor.Fiber F.p U) (xU' yU' : Functor.Fiber F.p U')
        (a : xU.val ⟶ x.val) (b : yU.val ⟶ y.val)
        (a' : xU'.val ⟶ x.val) (b' : yU'.val ⟶ y.val)
        (ha : F.p.IsHomLift q a) (hb : F.p.IsHomLift q b)
        (ha' : F.p.IsHomLift (f ≫ q) a') (hb' : F.p.IsHomLift (f ≫ q) b')
        (c : xU'.val ⟶ xU.val) (d : yU'.val ⟶ yU.val),
        F.p.IsHomLift f c → F.p.IsHomLift f d → c ≫ a = a' → d ≫ b = b' →
        ∀ (z : {z : I.obj.obj.obj (op U) // p.app (op U) z = q})
          (z' : {z : I.obj.obj.obj (op U') // p.app (op U') z = f ≫ q}),
          z'.val = I.obj.obj.map f.op z.val →
          (e U' (f ≫ q) xU' yU' a' b' ha' hb' z').hom.val ≫ d =
            c ≫ (e U q xU yU a b ha hb z).hom.val) :
    MapIsLocally (@LocallyOfFiniteType)
      (ObjectProperty.homMk ⟨p⟩ : I ⟶ schemeSpace T) := by
  sorry

/-- For two objects on locally finite type schemes, the space of triples has locally
finite type maps to their fibre product and to either scheme, on every etale chart.

Source: Stacks Project, Artin's Axioms, Tag 0CXM (lemma-base-change-versal), first proof
paragraph, using Tag 0CXI (blueprint: lem-sfb-limit-preserving-isom-space-lft).

The objects x and y are given by their cartesian sections over h_U and h_V. This is the
fibred Yoneda encoding of arbitrary fibre objects, with all pullback identifications.
Both vertical natural isomorphisms pin the projections of the representing equivalence.

Proof: (1) Identify the diagonal fibre with Isom by (c,u,v) mapping to v/u and inverse
delta mapping to (a,id,delta). This identifies its representing algebraic space.
(2) Isomorphism descent supplies the relative object-descent condition for the diagonal:
a descended delta_j gives (a_j,id,delta_j), compatible with alpha=u inverse at the limit.
The representable criterion lem-sfb-representable-lfp-object-limit-test gives local
finite presentation.
(3) Forget the finitely many relations in a finite presentation to obtain local finite
type on the same charts, by lem-sfb-space-local-properties-chart-test.
(4) Over U times_S V use the Isom space of the two pulled-back objects. Its functor of
points is exactly (a,b,alpha), so it represents the displayed 2-fibre product, with
both projections pinned. The map to the scheme fibre product is locally of finite
type by (3). Its scheme projections are base changes of U -> S and V -> S, so
lem-sfb-stack-finite-type-calculus gives local finite type of both composites.
Finally apply lem-sfb-space-etale-presentation-property-criterion and
lem-sfb-scheme-etale-source-target-properties with the identity target charts to get
the two scheme composites for every etale chart W -> Z, including nonsurjective ones. -/
theorem limit_preserving_isom_space_fibreProduct {S : Scheme.{u}}
    (F : BasedCategory.{v, w} (Over S)) (hF : IsFibredInGroupoids F)
    (hLimits : FibredGroupoidLimit.IsLimitPreserving F)
    (hDiagonal : HasAlgebraicSpaceDiagonal F)
    (U V : Over S) [LocallyOfFiniteType U.hom] [LocallyOfFiniteType V.hom]
    (x : BasedFunctor (discreteModuli (yoneda.obj U)) F)
    (y : BasedFunctor (discreteModuli (yoneda.obj V)) F) :
    ∃ (Z : AlgebraicSpace S) (p : Z.obj.obj ⟶ yoneda.obj (U ⨯ V)),
      (∃ e : BasedFunctor (discreteModuli Z.obj.obj) (moduliTwoFiberProduct x y),
        e.toFunctor.IsEquivalence ∧
        Nonempty (ModuliTwoIso (e.comp (moduliTwoFiberFst x y))
          (discreteModuliMap (p ≫ yoneda.map (Limits.prod.fst : U ⨯ V ⟶ U)))) ∧
        Nonempty (ModuliTwoIso (e.comp (moduliTwoFiberSnd x y))
          (discreteModuliMap (p ≫ yoneda.map (Limits.prod.snd : U ⨯ V ⟶ V))))) ∧
      MapIsLocally (@LocallyOfFiniteType)
        (ObjectProperty.homMk ⟨p⟩ : Z ⟶ schemeSpace (U ⨯ V)) ∧
      MapIsLocally (@LocallyOfFiniteType)
        (ObjectProperty.homMk ⟨p ≫ yoneda.map (Limits.prod.fst : U ⨯ V ⟶ U)⟩ :
          Z ⟶ schemeSpace U) ∧
      MapIsLocally (@LocallyOfFiniteType)
        (ObjectProperty.homMk ⟨p ≫ yoneda.map (Limits.prod.snd : U ⨯ V ⟶ V)⟩ :
          Z ⟶ schemeSpace V) ∧
      ∀ (W : Over S) (b : yoneda.obj W ⟶ Z.obj.obj), AlgebraicSpace.IsEtale b →
        LocallyOfFiniteType
          (yoneda.preimage (b ≫ p ≫ yoneda.map (Limits.prod.fst : U ⨯ V ⟶ U))).left ∧
        LocallyOfFiniteType
          (yoneda.preimage (b ≫ p ≫ yoneda.map (Limits.prod.snd : U ⨯ V ⟶ V))).left := by
  sorry

end CategoryTheory
